Shipped the same day, as `tools/release-stats.js` plus four lines in `tools/release.sh`. The release
script now counts the release it has just written an entry for, between that entry and the commit, so
from the next release onwards every entry carries `added`, `removed` and `logBytes`. The two counts are
`git diff --numstat` from one release's tag to the next and nothing else, over `index.html`, `src/`,
